  // Crashes: every feature ridden and every 10 m of trail is a small chance to crash (parts per million), scaled by
  // factors in permille: difficulty above the rider's skill (+overSkillPer100Permille per 100 points, lower for easy
  // stuff), jumps, worn features (below the rough level, up to 1 + wornFactor at 0 %), wet ground and tired riders.
  // Collisions are no chance: two riders passing a crossing of their ways (or of a way and the T-bar track) who are both
  // within collisionDistanceCm of it at the same moment crash, if at least one rides collisionMinSpeedCmPerS or faster. A crash is serious with
  // seriousBase + extras (jumps, collisions, over skill): the rider lies on the trail, blocking it, until the rescue
  // helicopter (public service) has flown them out; otherwise they ride down slowly and go home. A rider hurt while
  // being pulled up a T-bar stops the whole lift: for towStopMinutes (minor: they get off the track and go home) or
  // until the helicopter has flown them out (serious). Crashes cost no money: a crash closes its trail to new riders
  // (minorCloseMinutes, a serious one until the rescue). Each trail's crashes per 10 000 runs over the last rateDays
  // (counted over at least rateMinRuns) are compared with expectedCrashesPer10kRunsByRating: a guest who rode a trail
  // above it rates safety safetyLossPerExtraCrashPer10k permille lower per extra crash (worst trail, at most maxRateSafetyLoss).
  // bikeOnlyPermille: that share of minor crashes only break the bike (fixed in a bike shop's workshop, else the rider goes home).
  "crashRules": {
    "bikeOnlyPermille": 350,
